Genesis 3.text:
And unto Adam he said, Because thou hast hearkened unto the voice of thy wife, and hast eaten of the tree, of which I commanded thee, saying, Thou shalt not eat of it: cursed
is the ground for thy sake; in sorrow shalt thou eat
of it all the days of thy life;

Exodus 12.text:
And they shall eat the flesh in that night, roast with fire, and unleavened bread;
and with bitter
herbs they shall eat it.

And thus shall ye eat it;
with your loins girded, your shoes on your feet, and your staff in your hand; and ye shall eat it in haste: it
is the LORD’S passover.

Exodus 20.text:
Thou shalt not bow down thyself to them, nor serve them: for I the LORD thy God
am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children unto the third and fourth
generation of them that hate me;

Numbers 5.text:
And a man lie with her carnally, and it be hid from the eyes of her husband, and be kept close, and she be defiled, and
there be no witness against her, neither she be taken
with the manner;

This
is the law of jealousies, when a wife goeth aside
to another instead of her husband, and is defiled;

Numbers 13.text:
And see the land, what it
is; and the people that dwelleth therein, whether they
be strong or weak, few or many;

Numbers 15.text:
And when thou preparest a bullock
for a burnt offering, or
for a sacrifice in performing a vow, or peace offerings unto the LORD:

Joshua 9.text:
And it came to pass, when all the kings which
were on this side Jordan, in the hills, and in the valleys, and in all the coasts of the great sea over against Lebanon, the Hittite, and the Amorite, the Canaanite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite, heard
thereof;

Joshua 11.text:
But
as for the cities that stood still in their strength, Israel burned none of them, save Hazor only;
that did Joshua burn.

Joshua 12.text:
And these
are the kings of the country which Joshua and the children of Israel smote on this side Jordan on the west, from Baal-gad in the valley of Lebanon even unto the mount Halak, that goeth up to Seir; which Joshua gave unto the tribes of Israel
for a possession according to their divisions;

Joshua 13.text:
From Aroer, that
is upon the bank of the river Arnon, and the city that
is in the midst of the river, and all the plain of Medeba unto Dibon;

And their coast was from Aroer, that
is on the bank of the river Arnon, and the city that
is in the midst of the river, and all the plain by Medeba;

Joshua 14.text:
And the name of Hebron before
was Kirjath-arba;
which Arba was a great man among the Anakims. And the land had rest from war.

Joshua 15.text:
This then was the lot of the tribe of the children of Judah by their families;
even to the border of Edom the wilderness of Zin southward
was the uttermost part of the south coast.

2 Kings 19.text:
Have the gods of the nations delivered them which my fathers have destroyed;
as Gozan, and Haran, and Rezeph, and the children of Eden which
were in Thelasar?

2 Kings 22.text:
But to the king of Judah which sent you to enquire of the LORD, thus shall ye say to him, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel,
As touching
 the words which thou hast heard;

2 Kings 24.text:
Surely at the commandment of the LORD came
this upon Judah, to remove
them out of his sight, for the sins of Manasseh, according to all that he did;

2 Kings 25.text:
And it came to pass in the seven and thirtieth year of the captivity of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the twelfth month, on the seven and twentieth
day of the month,
that Evil-merodach king of Babylon in the year that he began to reign did lift up the head of Jehoiachin king of Judah out of prison;

1 Chronicles 6.text:
And they gave unto them,
of the cities of refuge, Shechem in mount Ephraim with her suburbs;
they gave also Gezer with her suburbs,

1 Chronicles 9.text:
And the porters
were, Shallum, and Akkub, and Talmon, and Ahiman, and their brethren: Shallum
was the chief;

Ezra 3.text:
They kept also the feast of tabernacles, as
it is written, and
offered the daily burnt offerings by number, according to the custom, as the duty of every day required;

Ezra 4.text:
Then they came to Zerubbabel, and to the chief of the fathers, and said unto them, Let us build with you: for we seek your God, as ye
do;
 and we do sacrifice unto him since the days of Esar-haddon king of Assur, which brought us up hither.

Job 27.text:
As God liveth,
who hath taken away my judgment; and the Almighty,
who hath vexed my soul;

All the while my breath
is in me, and the spirit of God
is in my nostrils;

Job 28.text:
The flood breaketh out from the inhabitant;
even the waters
 forgotten of the foot: they are dried up, they are gone away from men.

Job 29.text:
When his candle shined upon my head,
and when by his light I walked
through darkness;

As I was in the days of my youth, when the secret of God
was
 upon my tabernacle;

Job 31.text:
If I beheld the sun when it shined, or the moon walking
in
 brightness;

Job 33.text:
He looketh upon men, and
if any say, I have sinned, and perverted
that which was right, and it profited me not;

Job 39.text:
She is hardened against her young ones, as though
they were
 not hers: her labour is in vain without fear;

Job 41.text:
He maketh a path to shine after him;
one would think the deep
to be hoary.

Psalms 45.text:
Thine arrows
are sharp in the heart of the king’s enemies;
whereby the people fall under thee.

And the daughter of Tyre
shall be there with a gift;
even the rich among the people shall intreat thy favour.

Psalms 47.text:
For the LORD most high
is terrible;
he is a great King over all the earth.

Psalms 57.text:
Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens;
let thy glory
be above all the earth.

Psalms 62.text:
He only
is my rock and my salvation;
he is my defence; I shall not be greatly moved.

Trust in him at all times;
ye people, pour out your heart before him: God
is a refuge for us. Selah.

Psalms 114.text:
Ye mountains,
that ye skipped like rams;
and ye little hills, like lambs?

Psalms 132.text:
How he sware unto the LORD,
and vowed unto the mighty
God of Jacob;

Song of Solomon 2.text:
The flowers appear on the earth; the time of the singing
of birds
 is come, and the voice of the turtle is heard in our land;

Song of Solomon 4.text:
Thou
art all fair, my love;
there is no spot in thee.

Isaiah 44.text:
Thus saith the LORD, thy redeemer, and he that formed thee from the womb, I
am the LORD that maketh all
things; that stretcheth forth the heavens alone; that spreadeth abroad the earth by myself;

Isaiah 48.text:
Because I knew that thou
art obstinate, and thy neck
is an iron sinew, and thy brow brass;

Isaiah 51.text:
Therefore the redeemed of the LORD shall return, and come with singing unto Zion; and everlasting joy
shall be upon their head: they shall obtain gladness and joy;
and sorrow and mourning shall flee away.

Jeremiah 40.text:
Now when all the captains of the forces which
were in the fields,
even they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam governor in the land, and had committed unto him men, and women, and children, and of the poor of the land, of them that were not carried away captive to Babylon;

Likewise when all the Jews that
were in Moab, and among the Ammonites, and in Edom, and that
were in all the countries, heard that the king of Babylon had left a remnant of Judah, and that he had set over them Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan;

Daniel 3.text:
Now if ye be ready that at what time ye hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and dulcimer, and all kinds of musick, ye fall down and worship the image which I have made;
well: but if ye worship not, ye shall be cast the same hour into the midst of a burning fiery furnace; and who
is that God that shall deliver you out of my hands?

Daniel 4.text:
And whereas the king saw a watcher and an holy one coming down from heaven, and saying, Hew the tree down, and destroy it; yet leave the stump of the roots thereof in the earth, even with a band of iron and brass, in the tender grass of the field; and let it be wet with the dew of heaven, and
let his portion
be with the beasts of the field, till seven times pass over him;

Daniel 7.text:
Then I would know the truth of the fourth beast, which was diverse from all the others, exceeding dreadful, whose teeth
were of iron, and his nails
of brass;
which devoured, brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with his feet;

Zechariah 10.text:
Ask ye of the LORD rain in the time of the latter rain;
so
 the LORD shall make bright clouds, and give them showers of rain, to every one grass in the field.

Luke 23.text:
And, behold,
there was a man named Joseph, a counsellor;
and he was a good man, and a just:

John 5.text:
For as the Father raiseth up the dead, and quickeneth
them;
 even so the Son quickeneth whom he will.

Romans 15.text:
Now I beseech you, brethren, for the Lord Jesus Christ’s sake, and for the love of the Spirit, that ye strive together with me in
your
 prayers to God for me;

1 Timothy 3.text:
Likewise
must the deacons
be grave, not doubletongued, not given to much wine, not greedy of filthy lucre;

1 Timothy 5.text:
Rebuke not an elder, but intreat
him as a father;
and
 the younger men as brethren;

Revelation 21.text:
And the foundations of the wall of the city
were garnished with all manner of precious stones. The first foundation
was jasper; the second, sapphire; the third, a chalcedony; the fourth, an emerald;
